{
  "id": "kth-largest-element-in-an-array",
  "questionId": "kth-largest-element-in-an-array",
  "slug": "kth-largest-element-in-an-array",
  "title": "Kth Largest Element in an Array",
  "difficulty": "Easy",
  "category": "Heap",
  "patterns": [
    "heap",
    "top k",
    "min-heap"
  ],
  "lists": [
    "interview-150"
  ],
  "hints": [
    "you don't need the whole array sorted, you only need to know the kth largest value - can you avoid fully sorting?",
    "what if you kept a running collection of only the k largest values seen so far?",
    "a min-heap of size k lets you cheaply discard anything smaller than the current smallest of your top-k candidates",
    "push every number onto a min-heap; whenever the heap grows past size k, pop the smallest. after processing everything, the heap's smallest remaining value is the kth largest"
  ],
  "commonMistakes": [
    "using a max-heap of the whole array and popping k times, which works but is less efficient than a bounded min-heap of size k",
    "off-by-one: confusing the kth largest with the kth smallest, or with index k instead of k - 1 after sorting",
    "not handling duplicate values correctly by accidentally deduplicating before counting"
  ],
  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You're given a list of integers and a number `k`, counting from the\nlargest (so k = 1 means the single largest value, k = 2 means the\nsecond largest, and so on).\n\n**Find the `k`th largest value in the list.**\n\nDuplicate values count separately, so if the list is [5, 5, 3] then the\n1st largest is 5 and the 2nd largest is also 5.\n",
    "constraints": [
      "1 <= k <= nums.length <= 10^5",
      "-10^6 <= nums[i] <= 10^6"
    ],
    "notes": [
      "k equals the length of the array (the smallest value overall)",
      "k = 1 (the maximum value)",
      "all values in the array are identical",
      "single-element array"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Arguments passed into solution function",
    "outputFormat": "Return output matching method signature",
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "nums = [3, 2, 1, 5, 6, 4], k = 2",
        "output": "5",
        "expectedOutput": "5",
        "explanation": "sorted descending the list is [6, 5, 4, 3, 2, 1], so the 2nd largest is 5"
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_2",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "nums = [3, 2, 3, 1, 2, 4, 5, 5, 6], k = 4",
        "output": "4",
        "expectedOutput": "4",
        "explanation": "sorted descending: [6, 5, 5, 4, 3, 3, 2, 2, 1], the 4th value is 4"
      },
